Privacy Policy for Kage Player

This policy covers the Kage Player app.

Kage Player does not collect, sell or share your personal information. It has no accounts, no ads and no analytics or tracking tools. Your watch history, playlists and settings are stored only on your device.

The app asks for access to the videos on your device so it can list and play them, and it may show a notification while it plays in the background. These permissions are used only for playback.

Kage Player is free, open-source software. You can read the source code and report problems at https://github.com/OrewaTokyo/Kage-Player/issues

If this policy changes, the new version will be posted on this page and takes effect immediately. The Terms & Conditions inside the app have their own version number, and you will be asked to accept them again if they change.

Last updated: November 2026.
